# Contributor: FeralOS <dev@feralos.org>
# Maintainer: FeralOS <dev@feralos.org>
# greetd-config: the COMMON greetd configuration as an APK package (ADR-013).
# Only the parts shared by the niri and niriWayle sessions live here: vt 7
# (Alpine's default VT 1 collides with getty@tty1), a 3-line dispatcher
# (/etc/greetd/greeter.sh) that execs the DE script, the ReGreet config and
# the SHARED greeter provisioning. The DE-specific script
# ships with the DE config package: dms-config (greeter-niri.sh) / wayle-config
# (greeter-wayle.sh) — distinct filenames, so the packages never collide as
# apk content even though the DEs are mutually exclusive on an install. COSMIC does NOT use this file — its greetd config is
# cosmic-greeter-config (/etc/greetd/feralos-cosmic-greeter.toml, passed
# explicitly by the wrapper).
# regreet.toml = ONE SHARED FILE for both DEs (OWNER RULE 2026-11-25:
# AESTHETIC config always MERGES, FUNCTIONAL config stays separate —
# fonts/background/greeting are aesthetic so the file is identical; the
# portals pins and the PAM stacks are functional so those are per-variant).
# DejaVu Sans because it is in BOTH DE font sets (Cantarell is not in the
# Wayle set — a missing font forces full fontconfig fallback on every
# greeter start, the slow-boot contributor). The [widget.clock] timezone
# key is OMITTED on purpose: regreet then uses the SYSTEM time zone
# (sample: "Remove to use the system time zone"), which the installer sets
# from variables — one less variables-dependent seed (2026-11-24, D-A).# post-install: the SHARED greeter provisioning both desktop setups ran
# identically (greeter user, dirs, fontconfig USER-cache pre-build).
pkgname=greetd-config
pkgver=0.2.0
pkgrel=0
pkgdesc="FeralOS common greetd configuration (vt 7, greeter.sh entry point)"
url="https://github.com/skea999/feralos-aports"
arch="noarch"
license="ISC"
depends="greetd"
makedepends=""
source="config.toml greeter.sh regreet.toml greetd-config.post-install"
install="$pkgname.post-install"
options="!check" # static config, proven live by the greetd/greeter harness checks

package() {
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir/config.toml" "$pkgdir/etc/greetd/config.toml"
	# dispatcher: execs the DE greeter script (distinct filenames per DE so
	# the config packages never collide as apk content)
	install -Dm755 "$srcdir/greeter.sh" "$pkgdir/etc/greetd/greeter.sh"
	install -Dm644 "$srcdir/regreet.toml" "$pkgdir/etc/greetd/regreet.toml"
}
